<title>UK: EBRD provides finance for Moldova oil terminal. [CORRECTED 16:19 GMT]</title>
<headline>EBRD provides finance for Moldova oil terminal. [CORRECTED 16:19 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Bank for Reconstruction and Development said on Friday it would provide a $28 million (corrects from $19 million) financing package to construct a river-port oil terminal in Moldova.</p>
<p>The finance will go to Terminal S.A., a joint venture between state oil firm Tirex-Petrol, and Technovax SA of Greece.</p>
<p>Total cost of the project, on the River Danuba in south Moldova, is put at $38 million.</p>
<p>-- Jonathan Thatcher, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7770 (fax +44 171 583 7239)</p>
